  "worked_solution": "According to PEMDAS, we should first calculate the expression inside the **P**arentheses: $({5}^{2}-1).$\n\n To evaluate $({5}^{2}-1)$ we should also apply PEMDAS. We start with the **E**xponents:\n\n$$\n\\overset{25}{\\overset{⏞}{{5}^{2}}}-1=25-1\n$$\n\nThen, we perform the **S**ubtraction:\n\n$$\n25-1=24\n$$\n\nSo we have:\n\n$$\n{{({5}^{2}-1)}_{⏟}}_{24}\\,÷8=24÷\\,8\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we perform the **D**ivision:\n\n$$\n24÷8=3\n$$",
